From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:22:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 71/73] backends: follow Kestrel's pen settings

Read the pressure curves, the side buttons and the eraser button of
every pen from com.lantharos.kestrel.pen instead of a relocatable
org.gnome.desktop.peripherals.tablet.stylus schema per tool serial, so
one choice in Settings covers every pen people use, including one that
reports no serial.

Its button actions add to GNOME's: eraser makes the pen an eraser while
the button is held, as the other end of a pen would, by taking the pen
out of proximity and bringing an eraser for it in, lifting and pressing
the tip again around the switch when it is down. Screenshot, notes and
start reach the shell through the new MetaDisplay::pen-action signal,
and nothing makes a button do nothing at all.

Upstream-Status: luft-only follows Kestrel's settings instead of GNOME's
